  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Find the translation(s) that were applied to the graph of $x^2+y^2=9$ to give\n\n$$x^2+y^2-2x+8y=-8.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Translate 1 unit right and 4 units down.\n\nComplete the squares to obtain $(x-1)^2+(y+4)^2=9$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2+y^2-2x+8y&=-8\\\\\n(x^2-2x+1)+(y^2+8y+16)&=-8+1+16\\\\\n(x-1)^2+(y+4)^2&=9.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe replacements are $x\\mapsto x-1$ and $y\\mapsto y+4$. Translate the original circle 1 unit right and 4 units down.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
